

[38;5;231m⏺[39m Locked: static page, no server, banner when open + browser notification when backgrounded.

  Last thing I need before I can design: [1mwhat a task actually is.[0m This is the stored format, so it's the one decision
  that's genuinely annoying to change later — adding a field is easy, changing the shape of saved data means migrating
  whatever you've already typed in.

  The cheap-to-add-later group: notes, priority, tags. These are just extra fields on a record; bolting them on in a
  month costs nothing.

  The expensive one is [1mrecurrence[0m ("every Monday"). It changes what a task [3mis[0m — a repeating task isn't one record with a
  date, it's a rule that generates occurrences, and "complete" stops meaning "done" and starts meaning "done for this
  instance." It also doubles the reminder logic. If you want it eventually, I'd design the model to accommodate it now
  even if we don't build it; if you don't, we skip the complexity entirely.

  My recommendation: [1mtitle + due date + done, and nothing else.[0m Notes and priority are the two most commonly requested
  and least commonly used fields in a personal task app. Start minimal, let real use tell you what's missing — you'll
  know within a week, and adding then is trivial.

